# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for whichever provider you're
# using. Never commit the real .env — it's already in .gitignore.
#
# For anything beyond a solo laptop (a team, CI, a Kubernetes deployment), don't
# put real values in a .env file at all — inject them at runtime from a secrets
# manager (HashiCorp Vault, or your cloud's equivalent) instead.

# Pick ONE provider and set its key. The provider is chosen by the `model:`
# value in .groundtruth.yml (e.g. "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"), not by which of
# these variables happens to be set.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_API_KEY=
# AZURE_API_BASE=
# AZURE_API_VERSION=

# NVIDIA's API catalog (build.nvidia.com). LiteLLM reads this key, not
# OPENAI_API_KEY, for model: "nvidia_nim/<model>" or for the endpoint below.
# NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=

# Ollama needs no key at all — model: "ollama/<model>" and nothing below applies.

# Endpoints: where each stage's requests -- and its key -- are sent. Leave unset
# to call each provider's own default. These live here, next to the keys, and
# never in .groundtruth.yml: that file is in the repository under review, so a
# pull request could edit it and redirect your key to a server it controls.
#
# GROUNDTRUTH_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1     # review, and the default for all
# GROUNDTRUTH_VERIFY_BASE_URL=                                   # only if verify lives elsewhere
# GROUNDTRUTH_SUMMARY_BASE_URL=                                  # only if summary lives elsewhere

# --- Optional server mode (docs/server-mode-design.md) -- most people never
# set anything below this line. Ingest is opt-in and separate from the CLI.

# The database `groundtruth-server` (pip install "groundtruth-review[server]")
# writes reviews and findings to. No default: an unconfigured server refuses
# to start rather than guessing at a local connection nobody intended.
# GROUNDTRUTH_DB_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/groundtruth

# If set, /reviews requires this exact value as a Bearer token. Leave unset
# only on a server nothing but your own CI can reach.
# GROUNDTRUTH_INGEST_TOKEN=

# Set on a CI adapter (not on the server) to have it POST its JSON output
# here after posting to the pull request. Unset, nothing is sent anywhere.
# GROUNDTRUTH_INGEST_URL=https://your-server/reviews
